WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.840
The city of Seattle made history on Monday when it

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:03.380
raised the minimum wage.

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:05.720
The highest in the nation by far.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.540
Five years ago, Seattle became the first city

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.799
to pass a $15 minimum wage.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.120
I think it's pretty awesome since I benefit from it.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.300
A rising tide raises all boats?

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.780
15 in Seattle is just a beginning,

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:21.020
We have an entire world to win. Solidarity.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.480
[Crowd cheering]

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:24.340
When the law passed,

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:27.300
we went to Seattle to interview people about it.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.600
It's a good thing that we are leading the

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:30.900
way for the rest of the country.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.560
I wish that it was all over the place, not just Seattle.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.200
Increasingly, it is!

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.320
New York State taking steps towards

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.560
a $15 and hour minimum wage.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:44.560
Other states and lots of cities have copied Seattle.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:46.400
California governor Jerry Brown signed

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.180
a $15 minimum wage bill.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.780
But now the results from Seattle are in.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:52.960
Some people are being paid more.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.480
They are the winners.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.890
But for many people who wanted jobs…

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.080
The increased minimum wage is

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.770
having an opposite effect.

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:01.580
costing thousands of jobs and

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.159
actually hurting low income workers.

00:01:04.159 --> 00:01:05.280
You see it on this graph.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.220
The green line tracks the number of new jobs

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:10.060
created in Washington State.

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:13.140
The red line is new jobs in Seattle.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:17.420
Once Seattle raised its minimum wage to $15,

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:19.600
entry-level job growth stalled.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.940
It’s really presented by minimum wage advocates

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:23.680
as a win-win.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:27.480
It's a win-win for employers. It's a win-win for workers.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.289
And, there are no negatives.

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:31.340
But there are negatives, says Erin Shannon

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:33.400
of the Washington Policy Center.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.440
She points to stores like this one

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:38.440
where the owner used to hire kids and train them,

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:41.140
but once Seattle raised the minimum,

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:42.979
she stopped hiring beginners.

00:01:42.979 --> 00:01:44.359
[cash register]

00:01:44.359 --> 00:01:46.680
The politicians, in Seattle especially,

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.440
have no sense whatsoever about what it

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:52.060
means to small businesses like us.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:53.720
Most people we interviewed said

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:55.350
the politicians are right.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:56.860
Yes, some people will go out of business.

00:01:56.860 --> 00:01:58.629
Others will take their place.

00:01:58.629 --> 00:01:59.929
It's something we need to do.

00:01:59.929 --> 00:02:01.719
It’s as if they’ve never learned about

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.280
supply and demand.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:05.340
Minimum wage actually hurts my chances

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:06.720
of getting employed.

00:02:06.729 --> 00:02:09.200
This 20-year-old understands the effect better

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.140
than Seattle’s politicians did.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:13.260
Raising the minimum wage causes

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:15.019
increased unemployment.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:18.320
Rigel Nobel-Kosa is one of the $1500 winners

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:22.230
of a video contest done by my Classroom charity.

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:26.400
My name is Dillon Hodes and this is my WAGE RAGE.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.120
Dillon Hodes won the high-school video contest.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.560
He mentioned a friend who worked at Kroger

00:02:31.569 --> 00:02:35.220
until her store raised its minimum to 12 dollars

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.940
She was getting paid $12 an hour,

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:38.580
but slowly but surely,

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:41.680
they started cutting her days, her hours.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.380
She was regulated to only working on Sundays.

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:46.880
And that's because she was young and inexperienced.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:48.200
I feel the big thing-

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.040
She wasn't worth $12.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.740
She wasn't worth $12 to Kroger.

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:51.920
She's worth the world to me,

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.430
but she wasn't worth $12 to Kroger.

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:56.020
I learned things from their videos,

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:57.860
like how many wealthy countries

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:59.820
have no minImum wage

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.439
Countries such as Iceland, Norway, Sweden

00:03:02.439 --> 00:03:03.439
and Switzerland.

00:03:03.439 --> 00:03:04.380
Nobody knows that.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:06.670
No, no, and especially with Switzerland,

00:03:06.670 --> 00:03:09.100
Which has much lower unemployment than America,

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:13.050
partly because Switzerland has no minimum.

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:15.579
It stops us from actually getting a job

00:03:15.579 --> 00:03:17.920
Esther Rhodes won the high school essay contest.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:21.000
Her essay pointed out that America’s first

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.960
minimum wage laws were racist.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:25.760
At the time-- blacks were often paid less,

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:29.249
but they were more likely to be employed than whites.

00:03:29.249 --> 00:03:30.080
The whites were like,

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:32.540
"Hey, they're getting all the jobs. This isn't fair."

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:34.460
Congressman Allgood said he hoped

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:35.980
the min wage would stop:

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:39.660
“cheap colored labor in competition with white labor.”

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:42.040
So although Americans think the minimum

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:44.100
was invented to help needy people

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:45.540
It was meant for the opposite,

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:48.700
to keep the poor and the minorities from getting jobs.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:50.320
And today it still keeps

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.680
entry-level workers from finding work.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:55.940
But the politicians don’t understand the downside.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:58.880
Lift up the minimum wage to at least $15 an hour

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:01.780
Raising the minimum wage to 15 bucks an hour

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.340
[cheering]

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.960
It’s easy to see why a higher minimum wage

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:07.140
is so popular.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.880
On the surface, you think oh, this is a great idea

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:12.220
Because it raises some people’s wages.

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:15.000
Everybody deserves a living wage

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.980
But while it helps some, it harms many others.

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:19.400
Especially young people,

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:22.640
who now may not be offered their first job.

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:25.240
I'm 14, it'd be very difficult for me to find a job,

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.560
my labor wouldn't be worth $15 an hour.

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:30.640
If only politicians were as smart as those kids.

